 Text:RFD2484  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:02Z (RFD66606-2484) 'the import path for `seed/feed.db` into one store, and the counts, hashes and integrity check that verify the import.
 # tags: rfd:scope, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2484  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:03Z (RFD66606-2484) 'Can the challenge seed be loaded once into a store through the VFS, and verified?
 # tags: rfd:hook
 Text:RFD2484  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:04Z (RFD66606-2484) 'The seed file `seed/feed.db` is 238 MB: 50,000 users, 500,000 posts, and 2,016,005 likes, with its schema fixed by `schema.sql`. This table is also the 50 MB to 200 MB table that a sibling measurement needs. The seed is in WAL mode, but the VFS (the SQLite-on-FoundationDB virtual file system) needs `journal_mode=MEMORY` and `locking_mode=EXCLUSIVE`, and a 4 KiB page size, so the import cannot simply reopen the seed file as-is. The VFS already stages a commit too large for one FoundationDB transaction, which bounds one transaction to 10 MB, so SQLite's backup API or `VACUUM INTO` through the VFS may do the job without hand-chunking.
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2484  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:05Z (RFD66606-2484) 'Row counts per table match the file seed, a per-table content hash over an ordered `SELECT` matches the file seed, and `PRAGMA integrity_check` passes. A planted control, 1,000 posts dropped from the store after import, must be caught by the hash and the count.
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD2484  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-2484) 'Load the challenge seed into a store once, verified by counts and hashes
 # tags: rfd:details-title, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2484  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-2484) '- Look first for an existing import path in &{repo("datasource-store")}: `prove_big_commit.c`, `sqlrun.c`, `weft_sql.c`, `tpcc.c`, and `fly/backup-fresh.sh`; try SQLite's backup API or `VACUUM INTO` through the VFS before hand-chunking with `ATTACH` and rowid-ranged `INSERT ... SELECT` sized well under 10 MB.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2484  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-2484) '- Import the seed once, not at server start, with `journal_mode=MEMORY` and `locking_mode=EXCLUSIVE` set and a 4 KiB page size; record which path ran.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2484  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:09Z (RFD66606-2484) '- Verify with row counts per table against the file seed, a per-table content hash over an ordered `SELECT` compared with the file seed (reusing the content sha256 that `seed/make-seed.sh` prints, if it exposes one), and `PRAGMA integrity_check`.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2484  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:10Z (RFD66606-2484) '- Run the control: drop 1,000 posts from the store after import and confirm the hash and the count both catch it; record import wall time, bytes in the store, and `cluster.data.partitions_count` afterwards.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2484  1 LINE
 Text:Written

